cing--60);padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--60);padding-left:var(--wp--preset--spacing--60)\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><img decoding=\"async\" data-src=\"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/08\/kcl-logo.png\" alt=\"Kings College London\" class=\"wp-image-3895 lazyload\" style=\"--smush-placeholder-width: 263px; --smush-placeholder-aspect-ratio: 263\/199;width:150px\" width=\"150\" data-srcset=\"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/08\/kcl-logo.png 263w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/08\/kcl-logo-165x125.png 165w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 263px) 100vw, 263px\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB3aWR0aD0iMSIgaGVpZ2h0PSIxIiB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciPjwvc3ZnPg==\" \/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Learning about climate change by developing design skills<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Evaluation Report Summary of CCAC\u2019s demonstration programme<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"768\" height=\"488\" data-src=\"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/08\/ccac-kcl.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-3896 lazyload\" data-srcset=\"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/08\/ccac-kcl.jpg 768w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/08\/ccac-kcl-300x191.jpg 300w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/08\/ccac-kcl-315x200.jpg 315w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/08\/ccac-kcl-197x125.jpg 197w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 768px\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB3aWR0aD0iMSIgaGVpZ2h0PSIxIiB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciPjwvc3ZnPg==\" style=\"--smush-placeholder-width: 768px; --smush-placeholder-aspect-ratio: 768\/488;\" \/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Dr Melissa Glackin, Prof Heather King and Dr Lucy Wood<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Environmental Education Research Group<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Centre for Research in STEM Education<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>King\u2019s College London<\/strong><\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Throughout 2022, researchers from Kings College London (KCL), Melissa Glackin, Heather King and Lucy Wood evaluated the 5 Climate Change All Change co-design collaborations with primary schools. This entailed attending co-design classes, interviewing teachers, students and designer, analysing data, and drawing up their conclusions and recommendations.&nbsp; They provided a comprehensive main report and a summary report.&nbsp; An academic paper is in preparation.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">These reports were very supportive of the co-design model and the way it was delivered.&nbsp; The conclusions are underpinned by quotations from interviews. Helpful recommendations were made and CCAC has used these to refine the content of the current expansion programme.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">A download copy of the Summary Report is available from this website \u2013 see <a href=\"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/resources\/\">Resources<\/a>.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Evaluation reports covering the 5 co-design collaborations that took place in 2022 were delivered to CCAC at the beginning of the year.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":3893,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"_acf_changed":false,"footnotes":""},"categories":[7,12],"tags":[],"class_list":["post-2585","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","category-ccac-co-design","category-ccac-news"],"acf":[],"yoast_head":"<!-- 